; One view, and nothing else: `urn:iki:tutorial:live:picture` is another name for
; `urn:diagram:kernel`, which the host serves outside the dynamic space. `:resolve-at root` is
; what makes it a view: the rewritten name is asked from the root, under the caller's own
; capability, instead of inside this alias's empty child. view.ttl is the same declaration as
; the `ik:` Turtle core reads.
(alias
  (exact "urn:iki:tutorial:live:picture" "urn:diagram:kernel" :resolve-at root)
  (endpoints))
